## Task
@@STD_INTRO@@ @@README_GOAL@@ The agent drives the
robot only through the eai-standard/2.2 client (the simulator runs in the `sim` sidecar), which owns the scene and records
the episode as a (T, 14) trajectory of RoboDojo's own joint action at 25 Hz.

## Difficulty
@@DIFFICULTY@@ Here the agent sees only the three cameras (RGB, optional depth) and the arms' proprioception: no object
poses, no success signal, no reset, one episode (no step cap; RoboDojo's own evaluation gives a policy @@STEP_LIM@@ actions).

## Reference solution
@@ORACLE_SEE@@ RoboDojo releases no expert or planner script, and its training demonstrations record no
initial state, so none replays on a frozen layout. The task is reported separately until it has a positive example
(PROTOCOL §7, Open 4).

## Verification
The sim service ends the episode on RoboDojo's own check (success), a failed check, the runaway guard or the time limit, and
writes `/data/trajectory.npz`; the collect hook (`environment/sim/finalize.sh`) replays it from the frozen layout in two
fresh processes; `tests/grade.py` scores 1 iff @@STD_VERDICT@@. No oracle;
human review in PR #@@REVIEW_PR@@ (@@EVIDENCE_SHORT@@). `nop` (no actions) scores 0.

## Details
| | |
|---|---|
| Episode | one episode, no reset: it ends at the first action where RoboDojo's check passes, when a check fails for good, when the agent's time is up, or on a simulator error; no step cap (RoboDojo's evaluation gives a policy @@STEP_LIM@@ actions; a runaway guard at 15000) |
| Action space | `submit` chunks of `joint_position` (14: RoboDojo's own action at 25 Hz, the agent's `dt` a multiple of 1/25 s) or `ee_pose` (16: both arms' link6 targets, IK per row); `observe` frames or a watch window; `/kinematics` (FK / IK of both arms, stateless); binary RCB1 responses |
